  "notes": "COMPOSITION: {節|せつ} (economize, moderate) + {電|でん} (electricity).\n\nCONTEXT: {節電|せつでん} became especially prominent after the 2011 Tōhoku earthquake and Fukushima nuclear disaster, when Japan faced power shortages.\n\nCOMMON MEASURES:\n- Raising AC temperature in summer ({冷房|れいぼう} to 28°C)\n- Lowering heater temperature in winter ({暖房|だんぼう} to 20°C)\n- Turning off lights when not needed\n- Using LED lighting\n- Reducing standby power\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {省|しょう}エネ: energy saving (broader term)\n- {節水|せっすい}: water conservation\n- {節約|せつやく}: saving (general), economizing\n- {電力|でんりょく}{不足|ぶそく}: power shortage\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {節電|せつでん}する: to save electricity\n- {節電|せつでん}を{呼|よ}びかける: to call for power saving\n- {節電|せつでん}{対策|たいさく}: power-saving measures\n- {節電|せつでん}モード: power-saving mode",
